  "flags": [
    {"page": 1, "what": "The PDF prints no starting gold, only \"Max. Warband size is 15\". The template carries our 500 gc default."},
    {"page": 2, "what": "The Tomb Robber \"starts with Disarm/Spot traps skill\". That is our Trap Expert, so he is given it as a starting skill. See the decisions."},
    {"page": 3, "what": "The Skeletons' maximum characteristics (WS6 BS5 S4 T3 W2 I4 A4 Ld8) are the only ones printed for a skeleton anywhere in this batch, so they become a new race, Skeleton, which the Lahmian skeletons take too (their PDF prints none)."},
    {"page": 3, "what": "The undead rules are written \"Immune to physiology\", read as Immune to Psychology. The Skeletons are given Cause Fear, Immune to Poison, Immune to Psychology and May Not Run as printed, with no No Pain; the Undead Vulture's \"does not suffer from stun\" is No Pain."},
    {"page": 3, "what": "The Undead Golem costs 200 gc with an upkeep of 15 gc. A Henchman's upkeep is not something our templates hold, so it stays in his rules."},
    {"page": 3, "what": "\"This is Tuff Git's Flesh golem for Mordheim modified\" is the PDF's note on where the Golem comes from."},
    {"page": 4, "what": "The Scimitar (15 gc) and the Scythe (5 gc) are their own Khemri items now, with the rules the Khemri Equipment PDF prints; the Scythe is Scythe (Khemri), kept apart from the Sylvania scythes, and the Jambiya is our Dagger. The Ankus, the Cutlass and the Great Scimitar carry their rules too. All of them are declared on arabyan-nomads.json."},
    {"page": 1, "what": "No warband-wide special rules are printed; the Necromancer's succession note is his own rule."},
    {"page": 1, "what": "No group sizes are printed, and the Skeletons have no maximum."}
  ]
